-- 141: 80s POP MINING — TUNEPILE HOOKS OVER A 120 BPM GROOVE.
-- First session after the stack-ownership incident; the plugin's dead-end
-- "SC running outside this instance" refusal is fixed, so this is a normal jam.
-- Straight-ahead four-piece groove (kick/clap/hats/sub-bass) with three hooks
-- lifted from ~/tunepile, searched via index/tunepile.db (FTS5):
--   * arpeggio (d5)  — Tears For Fears, "Everybody Wants To Rule The World"
--       tabs-tidal/Tears_For_Fears_-_Everybody_Wants_To_Rule_The_World.gp4-*.tidal
--       riff as indexed: d5 fs5 a5 fs5 b5 fs5 a5 fs5 (D-major arpeggio, 1985).
--       cutoff now sweeps (slow 8, 1600..4400 sine) so the part opens on its own.
--   * melody (d6)    — a-ha, "Take On Me" (1985), opening synth line notes
--       tabs-tidal/Emil_Bulls_-_Take_On_Me.gp3-*.tidal (first-note extract).
--       Recast on our grid, RAMMED FORWARD (gain slow 16, 0.45..0.95 saw) — it
--       was mixed too quiet. Delay taps CLEANED OUT (ddSend 0): melody is dry.
--   * bass (d4)      — Michael Jackson, "Billie Jean" (1983) contour
--       tabs-tidal/Jackson_Michael_-_Billie_Jean.gp3-*.tidal — F#m root movement,
--       voiced on the project's dubsynth (sc/dubsynth.scd).
--   * pad (d11)      — vi-IV-I-V in F#m (Tunepile chords/progressions), hoRhodes,
--       ramped in (gain slow 16, 0.3..0.62 saw). This is the "new part".
-- Claps: first pass was room 0.45 / sz 0.85 (far too intense), then modulated
-- (slow 8 sine 0.05..0.22); FINAL pass drops reverb entirely — dry clap,
-- room 0, sz 0.35 — for the progressive section.
-- Delay: the tap/dub delay (ddSend) is removed from all melodic parts (d5/d6/d11).
-- Sources: bd/cp/hh/ho Dirt-Samples + dubsynth, tapestab, hoRhodes (project DSP).
-- Mix: per-stream gain deliberate, master UNITY as in 139/140.
-- Verification: 138+ scsynth synths while running; recording
-- recordings/jam-20261004-1103.wav with change markers.
-- Per-stream gain/amp deliberate. Kick: originally bd(5,8); now the syncopated
-- "x x - - x x x - -" figure (9 steps), which drifts against the 8-step bass
-- for a lopsided push instead of grid four-on-the-floor.
setcps 0.5

d1 $ s "bd bd ~ ~ bd bd bd ~ ~" # gain 1.15 # shape 0.25

d2 $ s "~ cp ~ cp" # gain 0.8 # hpf 350 # sz 0.35 # room 0

d3 $ s "[hh hh hh hh hh hh hh ho]" # gain 0.42 # speed 1.4 # pan 0.6

d4 $ note "fs2 ~ cs3 fs2 ~ e2 fs2 ~" # s "dubsynth" # waveMix 0.3 # cutoff 380 # fenv 2.4 # sustain 0.3 # gain 0.8

d5 $ note "d5 fs5 a5 fs5 b5 fs5 a5 fs5" # s "hoRhodes" # gain 0.5 # cutoff (slow 8 $ range 1600 4400 sine) # release 0.3 # ddSend 0

d6 $ slow 2 $ note "fs5 cs5 a4 e5 fs5 fs5 d5 b4 b4 e5 e5 gs5 gs5 a5 ~ ~" # s "hoRhodes" # gain (slow 16 $ range 0.45 0.95 saw) # cutoff 3800 # release 0.4 # ddSend 0

d7 $ silence

d8 $ silence

d9 $ silence

d10 $ silence

d11 $ slow 2 $ n "<[fs3,a3,cs4] [d3,fs3,a3] [a2,cs3,e3] [e3,gs3,b3]>" # s "hoRhodes" # gain (slow 16 $ range 0.3 0.62 saw) # cutoff 2400 # release 0.6 # ddSend 0

d12 $ silence
